{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This site uses the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","type":"reference"},{"text":". One command and it works,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because this is a Swift package with a single target.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In bigger projects the setup is not that simple. An Xcode project with many","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets, a framework whose docs live in a separate folder, a site that also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carries onboarding pages. In those cases the plugin is not enough and you have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to run ","type":"text"},{"code":"docc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" yourself.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Here is how I do it. Every step is implemented in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","type":"reference"},{"text":", a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"small package that only exists to be documented, so you can read the real","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"files instead of my snippets.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"The-two-halves","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The two halves"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"DocC can render two kinds of content.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Generated API reference."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Types and functions with their doc comments. You","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never write these pages. The compiler describes your module in a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", one JSON file per module, and DocC turns it into pages.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Manual documentation."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Articles and guides you write as Markdown inside a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"documentation catalog"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", a folder ending in ","type":"text"},{"code":".docc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Alone, neither is enough. The API reference says what a function returns, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not why the feature exists. The guide explains the idea, but cannot link into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the code. Putting them together is one flag. The rest is the work around it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"1-Write-the-doc-comments","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"1. Write the doc comments"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Generated pages are only as good as the comments in the code. A one line","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"summary, then details, then the parameters. Keep the summary to one sentence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because DocC reuses it as the subtitle in every list.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only ","type":"text"},{"code":"public","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols end up in the symbol graph, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never show up on the website.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"2-Add-a-catalog","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Add a catalog"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The catalog can live anywhere. It does not have to be inside a target, because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you pass its path to ","type":"text"},{"code":"docc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["doc\/","└── GardenKit.docc\/","    ├── GardenKit.md      # landing page","    └── Guides\/"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"DocC flattens the catalog and finds pages by file name, so the folders are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only for your own order. Keep the file names unique.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One page becomes the front door. If you title a file with the module name in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"double backticks, DocC merges it into the generated module page:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"becomes the overview and your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Topics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" groups set the order of everything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"below. That is what GardenKit and this site do.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-Get-the-symbol-graphs","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. Get the symbol graphs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now the generated half. Ask the compiler for symbol graphs while","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash","code":["xcodebuild build \\","    -scheme \"GardenKit\" \\","    -destination \"generic\/platform=iOS Simulator\" \\","    -derivedDataPath \"$build_dir\" \\","    -quiet \\","    OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS=\"\\$(inherited) -emit-symbol-graph -emit-symbol-graph-dir $symbol_graphs_dir\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Three details matter here.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"generic\/platform=iOS Simulator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builds for the simulator SDK without picking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a device, so codesigning never runs. A docs job has nothing to s","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\\$(inherited)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps the flags the project already sets. If you drop it, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module compiles differently and you will not notice right away.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"docbuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"xcodebuild docbuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" looks easier, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"documentation for the whole dependency tree. If one of those dependencies has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Objective-C headers, DocC’s header pass can fail with duplicate symbol errors","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the build stops. A plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" never runs that pass. It on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Swift symbol graphs, which is all DocC needs. This took me a while to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"figure out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"4-Keep-only-your-module","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"4. Keep only your module"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The build writes a graph for every module it compiled, including","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dependencies. If you pass all of them to DocC, your dependencies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your website:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash","code":["find \"$symbol_graphs_dir\" -type f -name '*.symbols.json' \\","    ! -name 'GardenKit.symbols.json' \\","    ! -name 'GardenKit@*.symbols.json' \\","    -delete"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both patterns are needed. ","type":"text"},{"code":"GardenKit.symbols.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has your own symbols.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GardenKit@Foundation.symbols.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an extension graph, one per module you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extend. Delete those and every ","type":"text"},{"code":"extension Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your code qui","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disappears from the site.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"5-Put-them-together","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"5. Put them together"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the command everything was preparing for:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash","code":["xcrun docc convert \"doc\/GardenKit.docc\" \\","    --additional-symbol-graph-dir \"$symbol_graphs_dir\" \\","    --fallback-display-name \"GardenKit\" \\","    --fallback-bundle-identifier \"com.example.gardenkit\" \\","    --output-dir \"$output_dir\" \\","    --transform-for-static-hosting \\","    --emit-digest"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"--additional-symbol-graph-dir","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the flag that merges the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol links in your articles resolve because of it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two ","type":"text"},{"code":"--fallback-*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" options give DocC the metadata Xcode would normally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass for a target. A catalog you convert by hand has no target, so they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"required. ","type":"text"},{"code":"--transform-for-static-hosting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes the output serv","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file host, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--emit-digest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the index the search needs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While writing, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"preview","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"convert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Same options,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost:8080","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and reloads when you save a Markdown file. It reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol graphs from the folder you already created, so there is no rebuild.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"6-Serve-it","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"6. Serve it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the site is not at the root of the domain, pass the prefix or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URL will be wrong:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash","code":["xcrun docc convert … --hosting-base-path \"docs\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"DocC does not write a root page either, so add a redirect:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash","code":["echo '<script>window.location.href += \"documentation\/gardenkit\"<\/script>' \\","    > \"$output_dir\/index.html\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That is the whole pipeline. I keep it in a script with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"-o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the docs are previewed locally, with it they are converted for hosting. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full version is ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh","type":"reference"},{"text":". In CI the output is just a folder of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"static files, so publishing it is a copy.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"Common-problems","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Common problems"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"Topic reference 'Plant' couldn't be resolved.","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The symbol graphs did"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not reach DocC. Check the path you passed, and that pruning did not delete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your own graph."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Extensions are missing."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"code":"Module@Other.symbols.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" graphs were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An internal type is missing."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Symbol graphs only contain public API."}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"Links","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Links"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"GardenKit","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GardenKit"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the example, with the full script"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit"},{"type":"text","text":", the symbol graph format"}]}]}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Building one documentation site from two sources: the API reference the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler generates, and the articles I write by hand."}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPipeline"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/releasenotes\/doccpipeline"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Haydar Karkin"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Combining Generated and Manual Docs"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"https://github.com/haydarKarkin/GardenKit":{"title":"GardenKit","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GardenKit"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit"},"https://www.swift.org/documentation/docc/":{"title":"DocC documentation","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC documentation"}],"url":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/"},"https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-docc-plugin":{"title":"swift-docc-plugin","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"swift-docc-plugin"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin"},"https://github.com/haydarKarkin/GardenKit/blob/main/scripts/generate_docs.sh":{"title":"in GardenKit","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"in GardenKit"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh"},"https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-docc-symbolkit":{"title":"SymbolKit","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SymbolKit"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit"},"https://www.swift.org/documentation/docc/formattinnt":{"title":"Formatting your documentation content","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Formatting your documentation content"}],"url":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt"},"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Senior iOS Engineer with 12+ years of experience shipping apps that people actually use —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from real-time messaging platforms to fintech, transit, and enterprise tooling."}],"url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes","role":"collection","title":"Haydar Karkin","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes"}}}